1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,410
Quantum computers have been on my mind a lot lately.
最近我常常想到量子计算机。

2
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:12,740
A friend has been sending me articles on how quantum computers might help solve some of the biggest challenges we face as humans.
一位朋友一直给我发文章，讲量子计算机可能如何帮助解决我们人类面临的一些最大挑战。

3
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:16,950
I’ve also had exchanges with two quantum-computing experts.
我还和两位量子计算专家交流过。

4
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:22,760
One is computer scientist Chris Johnson, who I see as someone who helps keep the field honest.
一位是计算机科学家克里斯·约翰逊，在我看来，他是帮助这个领域保持实事求是的人。

5
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,460
The other is physicist Philip Taylor.
另一位是物理学家菲利普·泰勒。

6
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:31,350
For decades, quantum computing has been little more than a laboratory curiosity.
几十年来，量子计算不过是实验室里的新奇玩意儿。

7
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:37,250
Now, big tech companies have invested in quantum computing, as have many smaller ones.
如今，大型科技公司已经投资量子计算，许多规模较小的公司也是如此。

8
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:46,070
According to Business Weekly, quantum machines could help us “cure cancer, and even take steps to turn climate change in the opposite direction.”
据《商业周刊》报道，量子机器可能帮助我们“治愈癌症，甚至采取措施扭转气候变化的方向”。

9
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:49,150
This is the sort of hype that annoys Johnson.
这正是让约翰逊恼火的那种炒作。

10
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:53,320
He worries that researchers are making promises they can’t keep.
他担心研究人员正在作出无法兑现的承诺。

11
00:00:54,120 --> 00:01:00,970
“What’s new,” Johnson wrote, “is that millions of dollars are now potentially available to quantum computing researchers.”
“新情况在于，”约翰逊写道，“量子计算研究人员现在有可能获得数百万美元的资金。”

12
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:12,560
As quantum computing attracts more attention and funding, researchers may mislead investors, journalists, the public and, worst of all, themselves about their work’s potential.
随着量子计算吸引越来越多的关注和资金，研究人员可能会就自身工作的潜力误导投资者、记者和公众，最糟糕的是，还会误导自己。

13
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:20,670
If researchers can’t keep their promises, excitement might give way to doubt, disappointment and anger, Johnson warns.
约翰逊警告说，如果研究人员不能兑现承诺，兴奋可能会被怀疑、失望和愤怒所取代。

14
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:24,980
Lots of other technologies have gone through stages of excitement.
许多其他技术也都经历过备受热捧的阶段。

15
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:35,960
But something about quantum computing makes it especially prone to hype, Johnson suggests, perhaps because “‘quantum’ stands for something cool you shouldn’t be able to understand.”
但约翰逊表示，量子计算有某种特质，使它特别容易被炒作，这或许是因为“‘量子’代表着某种很酷、你本就理解不了的东西”。

16
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:41,320
And that brings me back to Taylor, who suggested that I read his book Q for Quantum.
这又把话题带回到泰勒身上，是他建议我读读他的书《Q代表量子》。

17
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:46,160
After I read the book, Taylor patiently answered my questions about it.
我读完这本书后，泰勒耐心地回答了我关于这本书的问题。

18
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:52,100
He also answered my questions about PyQuantum, the firm he co-founded in 2016.
他还回答了我关于PyQuantum的问题，这家公司是他2016年与人共同创办的。

19
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:58,810
Taylor shares Johnson’s concerns about hype, but he says those concerns do not apply to PyQuantum.
泰勒和约翰逊一样担心炒作问题，但他说这些担忧并不适用于PyQuantum。

20
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:12,410
The company, he says, is closer than any other firm “by a very large margin” to building a “useful” quantum computer, one that “solves an impactful problem that we would not have been able to solve otherwise.”
他说，该公司比其他任何公司都更接近于造出一台“有用的”量子计算机，而且领先的“幅度非常大”；这种计算机能“解决一个影响重大、否则我们无法解决的问题”。

21
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:21,800
He adds, “People will naturally discount my opinions, but I have spent a lot of time quantitatively comparing what we are doing with what others are doing.”
他还说：“人们自然会对我的观点打折扣，但我花了很多时间，把我们正在做的事和别人正在做的事作了定量比较。”

22
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:28,580
Could PyQuantum really be leading all the competition “by a very large margin”, as Taylor claims?
PyQuantum真的有可能像泰勒声称的那样，正“以非常大的幅度”领先所有竞争对手吗？

23
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:30,200
I don’t know.
我不知道。

24
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,180
I’m certainly not going to advise my friend or anyone else to invest in quantum computers.
我当然不会建议我的朋友或其他任何人投资量子计算机。

25
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,890
But I trust Taylor, just as I trust Johnson.
但我信任泰勒，正如我信任约翰逊一样。
